   "text": {
    "L1": "Integers include negative numbers, zero, and positive numbers.",
    "L2": "On a number line, negatives go left of zero and positives go right.",
    "L3": "The spaces are equal, so −3 is three steps left of 0.",
    "L4": "Further right means greater. Therefore, −2 is greater than −7.",
    "L5": "For negative numbers, the larger number after the minus sign is the smaller integer.",
    "L6": "Every positive number is greater than every negative number, and 0 sits between them.",
    "L7": "To order −6, 2, −1, 0, and −4, read from left to right.",
    "L8": "The order is −6, −4, −1, 0, 2. Now choose the greater number."
   },
